.TH RECONSTRIKE 1 "2026-07-25" "ReconStrike-ng 3.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reconstrike \- Advanced Web & Network Vulnerability Assessment Framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reconstrike
.RB [ \-t
.IR TARGET ]
.RB [ \-\fIOPTIONS\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ReconStrike-ng
is a professional-grade vulnerability scanner designed for penetration testers,
security auditors, and DevSecOps teams. It performs comprehensive security
assessments against web applications and network endpoints using 43 specialized
scan modules.
.PP
Key features include:
.IP \(bu 2
43 vulnerability scan modules covering OWASP Top 10 and beyond
.IP \(bu 2
Zero false positive architecture with baseline comparison
.IP \(bu 2
Concurrent multi-threaded crawler
.IP \(bu 2
WAF/CDN detection (Cloudflare, AWS WAF, Akamai, Imperva, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Technology stack fingerprinting
.IP \(bu 2
Adaptive Network Masking (ANM) with Tor, proxy pool, MAC rotation
.IP \(bu 2
OWASP Top 10 & PCI DSS v4.0 compliance mapping
.IP \(bu 2
HTML, PDF, and JSON report generation
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Target Selection"
.TP
.BI \-t " TARGET" "\fR,\fP \-\-target " TARGET
Target URL (Required for DAST)
.TP
.BI \-\-sast\-dir " DIR
Local directory path for Static Application Security Testing (SAST)
.SS "Scan Profiles"
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " PROFILE
Scan profile: quick, standard, deep, aggressive, passive, api, owasp, full
.TP
.B
\-\-deep
Deep scan mode (shortcut for \-\-profile deep)
.TP
.B
\-\-full
Full scan: all modules, max depth, API scan, compliance, PDF report
.SS "Module Selection"
.TP
.BI \-\-modules " MODULES
Comma-separated list of modules to run
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-modules " MODULES
Comma-separated list of modules to exclude
.TP
.B
\-\-list\-modules
List all available scan modules and exit
.SS "Scan Configuration"
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " DEPTH
Crawl depth (default: 3)
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS
Request timeout in seconds (default: 10)
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " NUM
Number of threads (default: 10)
.TP
.BI \-\-rate\-limit " NUM
Max requests per second (0 = unlimited)
.SS "Authentication"
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-url " URL
Login page URL for authenticated scanning
.TP
.BI \-u " USERNAME" "\fR,\fP \-\-username " USERNAME
Username for authenticated scanning
.TP
.BI \-p " PASSWORD" "\fR,\fP \-\-password " PASSWORD
Password for authenticated scanning
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " FILE
Read password from file
.TP
.BI \-\-cookie " COOKIE
Custom cookie (format: name=value; name2=value2)
.TP
.BI \-\-header " HEADER
Custom header (format: Name: Value)
.SS "Proxy & Evasion"
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " PROXY
HTTP/SOCKS proxy (e.g., http://127.0.0.1:8080, socks5://127.0.0.1:9050)
.TP
.B
\-\-anm
Enable Adaptive Network Masking (auto-rotate identity on block)
.TP
.B
\-\-tor
Route traffic through Tor SOCKS5 proxy (127.0.0.1:9050)
.TP
.BI \-\-tor\-control\-port " PORT
Tor ControlPort for identity renewal (default: 9051)
.TP
.BI \-\-tor\-password " PASSWORD
Tor ControlPort authentication password
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy\-pool " FILE
File with newline-delimited proxy list for round-robin rotation
.TP
.B
\-\-rotate\-mac
Enable MAC address rotation (Linux, requires root)
.TP
.B
\-\-rotate\-ua
Enable User-Agent fingerprint rotation
.SS "Scope Control"
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-include " PATTERN
Regex pattern for URLs to include in scope
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-exclude " PATTERN
Regex pattern for URLs to exclude from scope
.TP
.B
\-\-no\-ssl\-verify
Skip SSL certificate verification
.TP
.BI \-\-user\-agent " UA
Custom User-Agent string
.SS "Output Options"
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-output " FILE
Output report file (default: reconstrike_report.html)
.TP
.BI \-\-pdf " FILE
Generate professional PDF report
.TP
.B
\-\-json
Output results as JSON to stdout
.TP
.BI \-\-json\-file " FILE
Save JSON results to file
.TP
.B
\-\-diff
Compare results with previous scan
.TP
.B
\-\-compliance
Include OWASP Top 10 & PCI DSS compliance report
.TP
.B
\-\-api\-scan
Enable API endpoint discovery and testing
.SS "CI/CD Integration"
.TP
.B
\-\-ci
CI/CD mode: exit code reflects severity (1=critical, 2=high, 3=medium)
.TP
.BI \-\-severity\-threshold " LEVEL
Minimum severity to report in CI mode: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW (default: MEDIUM)
.SS "Logging & Display"
.TP
.B
\-q\fR,\fP \-\-quiet
Minimal output (findings only)
.TP
.B
\-v\fR,\fP \-\-verbose
Verbose output
.TP
.B
\-\-no\-color
Disable colored output
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " FILE
Write log output to file
.TP
.B
\-\-version
Show version information and exit
.SH SCAN PROFILES
.TP
.B quick
Fast reconnaissance scan (5 modules, depth 2)
.TP
.B standard
Standard full scan (all modules, depth 3)
.TP
.B deep
Deep scan (all modules, depth 5, extra checks)
.TP
.B aggressive
Aggressive scan (all modules, depth 7, max coverage)
.TP
.B passive
Passive scan (no injection tests, no active probing)
.TP
.B api
API-focused scan (injection + auth + JWT modules)
.TP
.B owasp
OWASP Top 10 coverage scan
.TP
.B full
Maximum scan (all modules, depth 7, API scan, compliance, PDF report)
.SH EXAMPLES
Basic scan:
.PP
.RS 4
reconstrike \-t https://example.com
.RE
.PP
Deep scan with compliance:
.PP
.RS 4
reconstrike \-t https://example.com \-\-profile deep \-\-compliance
.RE
.PP
API-focused scan:
.PP
.RS 4
reconstrike \-t https://api.example.com \-\-profile api \-\-api\-scan
.RE
.PP
Authenticated scan:
.PP
.RS 4
reconstrike \-t https://example.com \-\-auth\-url https://example.com/login \-u admin \-p secret
.RE
.PP
With Tor proxy:
.PP
.RS 4
reconstrike \-t https://example.com \-\-tor \-\-anm
.RE
.PP
JSON output for automation:
.PP
.RS 4
reconstrike \-t https://example.com \-\-json \-\-json\-file results.json
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
No findings above threshold
.TP
.B 1
Critical findings detected
.TP
.B 2
High findings detected
.TP
.B 3
Medium findings detected
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/reconstrike/
Main application directory
.TP
.I /usr/share/reconstrike/scanner/
Scanner modules and core library
